{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "> p1(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*y) ^ 5\n> p2(x: u32, y: u32) = (y*x) ^ 5\n> q1(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y\n> q2(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y+1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "ucas", "ucas": "p1(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*y) ^ 5\np2(x: u32, y: u32) = (y*x) ^ 5\nq1(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y\nq2(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y+1", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "> p1(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*y) ^ 5\n> p2(x: u32, y: u32) = (y*x) ^ 5\n> q1(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y\n> q2(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y+1\n"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "> p1(x: u32, y: u32) = (x*y) ^ 5\n> p2(x: u32, y: u32) = (y*x) ^ 5\n> q1(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y\n> q2(x: u32, y: u32) = x*y+1\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "p1 and p2 are equal on the domain of p1 (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 35081 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)\n  polynomials of total degree at most 10, equal at 4 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 10/(2^61 - 1) = 4.34e-18 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 4 with at most 3.54e-70: equal over the integers except with that probability, and then for every input here (a probabilistic answer, not a proof)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "equiv", "ucas": "equiv p1 p2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": false, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "sampled", "sat": {"result": "gave_up", "aig_nodes": 35081}, "identity_test": {"result": "equal_probably", "error_probability": 3.5373746401666845e-70}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 35081 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps"}, "files": [], "text": "p1 and p2 are equal on the domain of p1 (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 35081 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)\n  polynomials of total degree at most 10, equal at 4 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 10/(2^61 - 1) = 4.34e-18 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 4 with at most 3.54e-70: equal over the integers except with that probability, and then for every input here (a probabilistic answer, not a proof)\n"}, "isError": false}}
